1
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:39,683
You have five minutes.

2
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:42,436
Go to the bathroom.

3
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:53,822
Where is 0864?

4
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:03,082
Thought we'd leave without you?

5
00:02:06,043 --> 00:02:08,253
You wouldn't last an hour out here.

6
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:10,214
The wolves would eat you alive.

7
00:03:19,742 --> 00:03:21,702
I hate having cellmates.

8
00:03:22,453 --> 00:03:24,580
Then we already have something in common.

9
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:27,541
The last one lasted a month.

10
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:30,544
I'll be here three days, tops.

11
00:03:31,295 --> 00:03:32,838
Everyone here is a lifer.

12
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,383
One more minute, and I'll let you take your
best shot.

13
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,930
Deal.

14
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:47,352
Can I sit with you in the dining hall?

15
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:48,437
No.

16
00:03:57,196 --> 00:03:58,781
This is a private area.

17
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,992
Fuck off.

18
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:09,166
Who do you think you are, asshole?

19
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,306
Now it's open territory.

20
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:37,319
The boss wants to see you.

21
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:46,912
So this is the one my men want to kill.

22
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,832
Do you know who I am?

23
00:04:50,374 --> 00:04:52,292
You're Semyon Chorney.

24
00:04:52,376 --> 00:04:54,545
Head of the Kirov Gang.

25
00:04:54,628 --> 00:05:00,175
Your weapons kill thousands of men, women and
children around the world.

26
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,928
You know me.

27
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:06,223
Who the hell are you?

28
00:05:07,391 --> 00:05:08,475
Me?

29
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:11,228
I'm a hunter.

30
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:14,773
He's a hunter.

31
00:05:15,983 --> 00:05:17,484
And what do you hunt?

32
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:24,032
People like you.

33
00:05:24,867 --> 00:05:27,244
The Hunter is a myth.

34
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:33,250
You're trapped, hunter.

35
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,502
What's your name? Who sent you?

36
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:38,464
My name is...

37
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:40,841
Kraven.

38
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,135
Kraven?

39
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:46,430
But you're not going to tell anyone.

40
00:05:59,401 --> 00:06:01,820
Every myth has a grain of truth.

41
00:06:01,904 --> 00:06:02,738
No.

42
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,503
Prisoner escaping!

43
00:06:21,465 --> 00:06:22,633
Prisoner escaping!

44
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,836
Three days.

45
00:06:58,919 --> 00:07:00,712
Three days.

46
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:18,439
He's getting away!

47
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:07,821
Go! Go! Go!

48
00:08:28,092 --> 00:08:29,176
You're late.

49
00:08:29,927 --> 00:08:32,846
Next time, you break out of prison and I'll
fly the plane.

50
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:33,931
No, thanks.

51
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:36,266
So, how did it go?

52
00:08:36,350 --> 00:08:38,185
Same as always.

53
00:08:39,103 --> 00:08:40,354
Good for me...

54
00:08:41,355 --> 00:08:42,731
bad for him.

55
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:58,247
We found a body.

56
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,046
Did you identify him?

57
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:14,763
It's prisoner 0864.

58
00:09:15,764 --> 00:09:18,517
Then who the hell killed Chorney?

59
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:32,781
KRAVEN THE HUNTER

60
00:09:35,701 --> 00:09:41,707
16 YEARS EARLIER

61
00:09:46,712 --> 00:09:50,966
ST. MICHAEL'S ACADEMY, UPSTATE NEW YORK

62
00:09:53,844 --> 00:09:55,888
Kravinoff and Kravinoff!

63
00:09:55,971 --> 00:09:58,182
Your father is coming to pick you up.

64
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:05,898
What did you do?

65
00:10:07,024 --> 00:10:08,275
Me?

66
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:09,777
Nothing. Wasn't it you?

67
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,028
No.

68
00:10:33,759 --> 00:10:35,219
Where are we going, Dad?

69
00:10:36,095 --> 00:10:38,388
- We're halfway through the school year.
- Sergei...

70
00:10:38,472 --> 00:10:40,307
Mom never did anything like this.

71
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:41,391
Sergei...

72
00:10:43,769 --> 00:10:45,395
Your mother is dead.

73
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:49,650
She took her own life. She was weak.

74
00:10:50,776 --> 00:10:52,736
Sick in the head.

75
00:10:57,116 --> 00:10:58,784
It was her choice.

76
00:10:59,952 --> 00:11:01,787
She died because you sent her away.

77
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:02,704
No.

78
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:05,999
She gave up long ago.

79
00:11:07,543 --> 00:11:09,795
You hadn't seen her in two years.

80
00:11:10,796 --> 00:11:12,506
Nothing will change for you.

81
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:16,552
- Or for you, Dmitri.
- Where are we going, Dad?

82
00:11:16,635 --> 00:11:18,053
To the funeral?

83
00:11:18,137 --> 00:11:21,432
If you take your own life, you don't deserve
that honor.

84
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:23,225
Then where are you taking us?

85
00:11:23,308 --> 00:11:24,726
We're going hunting.

86
00:11:25,477 --> 00:11:27,855
They spotted the lion again. The Tsar.

87
00:11:29,273 --> 00:11:31,316
It'll be good for you.

88
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,234
For both of you.

89
00:11:32,985 --> 00:11:34,319
Going out with men,

90
00:11:34,403 --> 00:11:36,029
being one with nature.

91
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,574
Shooting to kill.

92
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:41,118
Having fun.

93
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,966
NORTHERN GHANA

94
00:11:58,677 --> 00:12:00,095
Be careful with that.

95
00:12:00,179 --> 00:12:01,263
XIII DEATH

96
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:03,640
Put those cards away, Calypso.

97
00:12:03,724 --> 00:12:06,143
Your parents will be back soon.

98
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:08,896
And you know what they think about this.

99
00:12:08,979 --> 00:12:10,856
It's a game, Grandma.

100
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:14,151
Do you think my cards are just pretty pictures?

101
00:12:15,194 --> 00:12:17,279
Don't be so sure, Calypso.

102
00:12:17,988 --> 00:12:20,908
They show us the hidden path.

103
00:12:22,159 --> 00:12:25,245
What? They predict the future?

104
00:12:26,330 --> 00:12:27,956
In the right hands.

105
00:12:33,128 --> 00:12:35,506
Lay three cards on the table.

106
00:12:36,381 --> 00:12:38,926
The first card represents the subject.

107
00:12:39,718 --> 00:12:41,178
The High Priestess?

108
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:45,682
You come from a long line of very powerful women.

109
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:48,769
The second card is the situation.

110
00:12:49,937 --> 00:12:51,438
The Tower.

111
00:12:51,522 --> 00:12:54,441
There's going to be a terrible accident.

112
00:12:57,069 --> 00:12:59,738
The third card is the outcome.

113
00:12:59,822 --> 00:13:01,323
Strength.

114
00:13:01,907 --> 00:13:04,535
That card carries great danger.

115
00:13:05,077 --> 00:13:07,538
I'm going to give you something, Calypso.

116
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:10,290
I was going to wait until you were older,

117
00:13:10,374 --> 00:13:14,002
but the cards show you'll need it soon.

118
00:13:14,086 --> 00:13:15,629
What is it?

119
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:16,922
A potion.

120
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:21,844
The formula has been passed down in our family
for generations.

121
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:25,389
What does that symbol mean?

122
00:13:25,472 --> 00:13:28,392
It's the symbol of the spirit Papa Legba.

123
00:13:29,268 --> 00:13:32,312
He opens the gateway to the other side.

124
00:13:32,396 --> 00:13:34,064
Protect it.

125
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:36,859
It's very powerful.

126
00:13:38,444 --> 00:13:39,737
It's yours.

127
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:44,950
It will heal anyone who drinks it in
unimaginable ways.

128
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:47,911
The time is very near.

129
00:13:47,995 --> 00:13:50,122
You'll know what to do with it.

130
00:13:50,956 --> 00:13:54,501
Now put the deck away before your parents return.

131
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:13,729
Nice shot, Nikolai!

132
00:14:22,946 --> 00:14:24,073
Sergei.

133
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:32,706
Did you see that?

134
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:34,333
She's beautiful.

135
00:14:37,211 --> 00:14:38,837
Don't fear death.

136
00:14:39,963 --> 00:14:41,757
They are prey.

137
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,093
And we are predators.

138
00:14:50,891 --> 00:14:56,021
Man should be the only animal that poses a threat.

139
00:15:00,901 --> 00:15:04,196
Dmitri, don't be so weak.

140
00:15:05,781 --> 00:15:07,491
Be a man.

141
00:15:11,328 --> 00:15:13,038
Are you okay?

142
00:15:13,122 --> 00:15:14,123
Yeah.

143
00:15:16,041 --> 00:15:17,835
He shouldn't have spoken to you like that.

144
00:15:18,627 --> 00:15:19,962
You know...

145
00:15:21,255 --> 00:15:22,673
He's an asshole.

146
00:15:23,298 --> 00:15:25,384
There's nothing I can do about it.

147
00:15:25,968 --> 00:15:28,262
He'll never respect me the way he respects you.

148
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:30,806
Wanna bet?

149
00:15:40,274 --> 00:15:41,692
I miss Mom.

150
00:15:42,776 --> 00:15:44,194
Me too, Dima.

151
00:15:44,278 --> 00:15:45,487
Me too.

152
00:15:52,077 --> 00:15:55,539
- Was that the Tsar?
- It wasn't even a kitten.

153
00:15:55,622 --> 00:15:58,542
Maybe it was the Tsar's illegitimate half-brother.

154
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,879
- Like you, Dmitri.
- Leave the boy alone.

155
00:16:02,504 --> 00:16:06,258
It's not his fault his father has a wandering eye.

156
00:16:06,884 --> 00:16:09,136
You'll know the Tsar when you hear him.

157
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:13,390
He sounds like thunder on a mountaintop.

158
00:16:13,474 --> 00:16:15,559
Have you seen this beast?

159
00:16:16,143 --> 00:16:18,187
I've seen what he's done.

160
00:16:19,438 --> 00:16:24,193
That cat has killed two or three dozen men.

161
00:16:24,276 --> 00:16:25,110
Really?

162
00:16:25,903 --> 00:16:30,240
Ever since men like you came here to kill lions,

163
00:16:30,824 --> 00:16:34,078
there's been a legend of a lion no one can kill.

164
00:16:34,161 --> 00:16:35,662
Men like me.

165
00:16:36,497 --> 00:16:39,708
Yet you still take my money, don't you, Bahari?

166
00:16:40,542 --> 00:16:42,795
A lion hunts to eat.

167
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:45,464
So do I.

168
00:16:50,427 --> 00:16:52,387
Why do you hunt, Nikolai?

169
00:16:53,222 --> 00:16:54,681
You know why, Bahari.

170
00:16:56,266 --> 00:17:00,187
The man who kills a legend becomes a legend.

171
00:17:05,275 --> 00:17:06,360
Nikolai,

172
00:17:06,902 --> 00:17:08,195
we need to talk.

173
00:17:08,278 --> 00:17:09,655
Save your breath.

174
00:17:10,572 --> 00:17:12,241
No, it's a chronic condition.

175
00:17:12,324 --> 00:17:15,786
I'll be fine as long as I take the occasional
break.

176
00:17:15,869 --> 00:17:17,704
One thing you should know about me

177
00:17:17,788 --> 00:17:19,957
is that I always think about the future.

178
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,044
I want us to be partners.

179
00:17:26,088 --> 00:17:27,673
What's your name?

180
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,678
I'm Vladimir's guest.

181
00:17:34,096 --> 00:17:35,597
Aleksei Sytsevich.

182
00:17:35,681 --> 00:17:36,682
No.

183
00:17:37,808 --> 00:17:39,810
You have no name.

184
00:17:41,979 --> 00:17:45,232
In this world, you barely exist.

185
00:17:45,315 --> 00:17:49,236
What can a sick, nameless, nonexistent

186
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:51,488
idiot offer the Kravinoffs?

187
00:17:52,489 --> 00:17:53,615
Nothing.

188
00:17:55,159 --> 00:17:56,577
I came here...

189
00:17:57,703 --> 00:18:00,247
to teach my sons the joy of stalking prey.

190
00:18:01,248 --> 00:18:02,958
And you

191
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:06,378
and your idiotic voice are stalking me.

192
00:18:07,504 --> 00:18:08,839
So shut up.

193
00:18:18,348 --> 00:18:20,100
I hope Dad kills it.

194
00:18:21,226 --> 00:18:22,394
Why?

195
00:18:22,478 --> 00:18:25,981
Because then he'll become a legend and we'll
never have to come back.

196
00:18:29,276 --> 00:18:31,570
A legend would fight fair.

197
00:18:31,653 --> 00:18:32,988
Not with a rifle.

198
00:18:33,072 --> 00:18:35,866
He'd do it one-on-one, with the weapons he was
born with.

199
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:46,460
Dmitri,

200
00:18:47,419 --> 00:18:48,670
get behind me.

201
00:19:24,206 --> 00:19:25,791
Dmitri! Move!

202
00:19:25,874 --> 00:19:26,917
Move!

203
00:19:30,587 --> 00:19:32,172
Run!

204
00:19:34,716 --> 00:19:35,884
Run!

205
00:19:46,019 --> 00:19:47,521
Sergei!

206
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:51,775
Sergei!

207
00:20:12,713 --> 00:20:14,506
Calypso, look!

208
00:20:29,646 --> 00:20:31,648
Come on, sweetheart, stand up.

209
00:20:35,069 --> 00:20:36,361
Calypso?

210
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:39,573
Calypso?

211
00:20:42,367 --> 00:20:43,410
Calypso!

212
00:21:38,632 --> 00:21:43,095
In the name of all the spirits and all the
mysteries...

213
00:21:47,266 --> 00:21:48,517
Help!

214
00:21:53,105 --> 00:21:56,108
...bring forth the power of the earth.

215
00:22:07,786 --> 00:22:08,787
Wait.

216
00:22:19,423 --> 00:22:22,176
Bring forth the power of the stars.

217
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:32,352
Everybody clear. Shocking now.

218
00:22:37,733 --> 00:22:39,234
We did everything we could.

219
00:22:40,319 --> 00:22:42,696
I'm calling the time of death.

220
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:43,989
6:51.

221
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:15,604
XI STRENGTH

222
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:20,317
The rescuers found this card in your pocket.

223
00:23:20,401 --> 00:23:23,070
You're a very lucky young man.

224
00:23:23,612 --> 00:23:25,155
Thank you for saving me.

225
00:23:25,823 --> 00:23:27,699
I wish I could say it was me.

226
00:23:28,450 --> 00:23:30,244
But I didn't save you.

227
00:23:31,370 --> 00:23:33,038
I don't understand.

228
00:23:33,122 --> 00:23:34,998
That makes two of us.

229
00:23:35,082 --> 00:23:39,670
We'll run some tests, see if we can find out
what happened.

230
00:23:39,753 --> 00:23:41,422
Sergei.

231
00:23:41,505 --> 00:23:42,339
Dima.

232
00:23:49,054 --> 00:23:50,347
Why didn't you shoot?

233
00:23:52,558 --> 00:23:56,895
You must be Sergei's father, Mr. Kravinoff.

234
00:23:56,979 --> 00:23:58,730
I've come to take him home.

235
00:23:58,814 --> 00:24:01,400
He needs to stay here and recover.

236
00:24:01,483 --> 00:24:04,695
He was clinically dead for over three minutes.

237
00:24:04,778 --> 00:24:07,239
He's coming with me.

238
00:24:07,322 --> 00:24:11,201
OUTSIDE LONDON

239
00:24:22,254 --> 00:24:23,964
Sergei.

240
00:24:24,631 --> 00:24:27,676
I'm sorry we're not together, but we will be soon.

241
00:24:29,178 --> 00:24:33,766
You know I never wanted this,

242
00:24:33,849 --> 00:24:37,269
but it was the only way out your father gave me.

243
00:24:38,687 --> 00:24:43,108
Promise me you'll never become a man like him.

244
00:24:43,192 --> 00:24:46,737
Sergei! Come here!

245
00:24:51,909 --> 00:24:55,287
Dad is the only animal that poses a threat.

246
00:24:55,996 --> 00:24:57,873
You're getting good.

247
00:24:57,956 --> 00:24:59,541
You'll do well.

248
00:24:59,625 --> 00:25:02,127
You almost got your brother killed.

249
00:25:03,712 --> 00:25:07,758
You almost got yourself killed. Because you
were afraid.

250
00:25:08,926 --> 00:25:10,636
Fear devours you.

251
00:25:12,137 --> 00:25:14,056
It makes you weak.

252
00:25:15,224 --> 00:25:18,393
Are you weak like your mother? Crazy?

253
00:25:18,477 --> 00:25:20,687
Or are you like me?

254
00:25:20,771 --> 00:25:24,024
Because if you show your enemies weakness,

255
00:25:24,108 --> 00:25:27,361
you give them an opening.

256
00:25:28,904 --> 00:25:31,323
You're old enough to understand.

257
00:25:33,242 --> 00:25:35,869
You know what I do, don't you?

258
00:25:36,912 --> 00:25:40,332
One day, you'll be in charge.

259
00:25:40,416 --> 00:25:42,334
Dmitri, go.

260
00:25:43,210 --> 00:25:46,213
Dmitri will return to school in New York,

261
00:25:47,047 --> 00:25:49,049
and you will stay here.

262
00:25:49,716 --> 00:25:50,592
With me.

263
00:25:50,676 --> 00:25:54,263
America has made you soft.

264
00:25:54,346 --> 00:25:56,098
It's for your own good.

265
00:25:57,224 --> 00:25:59,643
Everyone has a path to walk.

266
00:26:01,770 --> 00:26:03,605
Accept your true self

267
00:26:04,398 --> 00:26:06,567
and you'll have the strength to walk it.

268
00:26:09,528 --> 00:26:10,696
Come.

269
00:26:11,697 --> 00:26:13,115
Come here.

270
00:26:17,703 --> 00:26:19,371
I brought you something.

271
00:26:25,794 --> 00:26:28,213
You'll never have to be afraid again.

272
00:26:39,808 --> 00:26:41,268
It should have killed you instead!

273
00:26:43,687 --> 00:26:44,855
What's wrong with you?

274
00:26:49,193 --> 00:26:51,070
Sergei! Come back here!

275
00:26:57,367 --> 00:26:58,535
Are you okay?

276
00:27:34,154 --> 00:27:36,615
PASSPORT - UNITED STATES OF AMERICA

277
00:28:35,632 --> 00:28:37,134
Don't leave me with him.

278
00:28:37,217 --> 00:28:38,343
I'm leaving.

279
00:28:39,094 --> 00:28:40,596
- I have to.
- Why?

280
00:28:40,679 --> 00:28:43,891
I can't explain it. Something happened to me.

281
00:28:43,974 --> 00:28:45,225
What are you talking about?

282
00:28:45,309 --> 00:28:47,519
Remember where we used to go camping?

283
00:28:48,562 --> 00:28:51,023
Where you could only hear crickets and owls?

284
00:28:51,648 --> 00:28:54,276
And Mom used to sing to us by the campfire?

285
00:28:54,359 --> 00:28:56,445
That land is all I have left of her.

286
00:28:56,528 --> 00:28:58,155
And that makes it okay?

287
00:28:59,156 --> 00:29:00,616
Just picture me there.

288
00:29:04,244 --> 00:29:05,788
I'm sorry, Dima.

289
00:29:06,705 --> 00:29:07,539
I really am.

290
00:29:11,460 --> 00:29:13,545
If you're going to leave, then leave.

291
00:29:15,672 --> 00:29:16,632
Go!

292
00:29:20,803 --> 00:29:22,513
I won't be gone forever.

293
00:29:32,231 --> 00:29:33,440
Where are you going?

294
00:29:34,358 --> 00:29:36,235
I want to get out of England.

295
00:29:36,318 --> 00:29:37,653
To Russia.

296
00:29:37,736 --> 00:29:38,862
In that thing?

297
00:29:40,114 --> 00:29:42,533
You know there are planes and trains, right?

298
00:29:44,243 --> 00:29:46,703
- Are you running away?
- Yes.

299
00:29:47,704 --> 00:29:49,081
That's right.

300
00:29:49,164 --> 00:29:50,624
Then get in. Let's go.

301
00:30:08,475 --> 00:30:13,230
WESTERN RUSSIA

302
00:32:29,867 --> 00:32:31,493
She was weak.

303
00:32:32,828 --> 00:32:34,538
Sick in the head.

304
00:32:34,621 --> 00:32:36,373
She died because you sent her away.

305
00:32:36,457 --> 00:32:37,666
Sergei!

306
00:32:38,459 --> 00:32:39,626
Run!

307
00:32:40,461 --> 00:32:41,670
Sergei!

308
00:32:43,797 --> 00:32:45,215
Fear devours you.

309
00:32:45,841 --> 00:32:47,676
It makes you weak.

310
00:32:48,719 --> 00:32:50,971
Everyone has a path to walk.

311
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:54,641
They are prey.

312
00:32:57,311 --> 00:32:59,354
And we are predators.

313
00:33:59,248 --> 00:34:03,502
Just the horns. Leave the rest.

314
00:34:28,152 --> 00:34:31,155
You don't belong here, kid. Go home.

315
00:34:36,952 --> 00:34:38,829
This is my home.

316
00:34:54,845 --> 00:34:56,263
Is this yours?

317
00:34:57,055 --> 00:34:58,432
Put it down!

318
00:34:59,475 --> 00:35:01,101
Or you're dead.

319
00:36:00,786 --> 00:36:05,040
PRESENT DAY

320
00:36:22,266 --> 00:36:23,976
Welcome home.

321
00:36:24,059 --> 00:36:26,437
We flew under the radar, as always.

322
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:28,188
Call me when you need me.

323
00:36:55,299 --> 00:36:57,843
Voicemail - (1) missed call

324
00:36:57,926 --> 00:37:00,554
Sergei, it's your father.

325
00:37:00,637 --> 00:37:02,723
Come home. I miss you.

326
00:37:02,806 --> 00:37:06,018
I'm sorry for everything that happened.

327
00:37:07,102 --> 00:37:09,396
Just kidding, it's your brother.

328
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:11,523
I texted you. Where have you been?

329
00:37:13,984 --> 00:37:16,653
Still hiding in the woods, huh?

330
00:37:17,279 --> 00:37:19,907
Will I see you on my birthday?

331
00:37:19,990 --> 00:37:21,617
Call me.

332
00:37:48,852 --> 00:37:51,480
Load this shit up!

333
00:37:52,106 --> 00:37:53,440
Hurry!

334
00:37:56,276 --> 00:37:57,903
Get them on the truck.

335
00:38:10,082 --> 00:38:10,916
Who is that?

336
00:38:16,296 --> 00:38:18,465
This is private property.

337
00:38:18,549 --> 00:38:22,761
I came to see if you were going to lock up
before you left.

338
00:38:25,556 --> 00:38:26,473
Move!

339
00:38:33,230 --> 00:38:34,898
Move.

340
00:38:34,982 --> 00:38:39,361
Why do you kill animals and only take their horns?

341
00:38:40,529 --> 00:38:41,864
Because.

342
00:38:44,575 --> 00:38:45,909
"Because"?

343
00:38:46,785 --> 00:38:47,745
Step aside.

344
00:38:47,828 --> 00:38:50,038
There are six of us and one of you.

345
00:38:50,998 --> 00:38:52,750
There are six of you now.

346
00:38:52,833 --> 00:38:54,543
I don't have time. I've got deliveries.

347
00:38:54,626 --> 00:38:55,878
Let's go!

348
00:39:05,971 --> 00:39:07,389
What the fuck?

349
00:39:21,570 --> 00:39:22,863
Come on! Come on!

350
00:39:47,387 --> 00:39:50,849
LONDON DOCKLANDS

351
00:39:54,311 --> 00:39:55,312
Mr. Taglin.

352
00:39:56,980 --> 00:39:58,774
I'm sorry.

353
00:39:58,857 --> 00:40:01,276
The guy came out of nowhere.

354
00:40:02,027 --> 00:40:04,029
Some crazy local or...

355
00:40:04,738 --> 00:40:06,490
I don't know.

356
00:40:06,573 --> 00:40:08,450
But I took care of him.

357
00:40:08,534 --> 00:40:10,160
He won't bother us anymore.

358
00:40:14,331 --> 00:40:17,042
In a moment, nothing will ever bother you again.

359
00:40:17,126 --> 00:40:18,502
How...?

360
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:21,547
Where's Mr. Taglin?

361
00:40:22,172 --> 00:40:24,174
Oh. You're standing on him.

362
00:40:27,678 --> 00:40:28,971
I found this.

363
00:40:29,054 --> 00:40:30,764
Interesting.

364
00:40:30,848 --> 00:40:31,974
You're a poacher.

365
00:40:32,057 --> 00:40:35,144
Mr. Taglin hires poachers. But these names...

366
00:40:35,853 --> 00:40:38,689
Drugs, weapons, trafficking...

367
00:40:39,356 --> 00:40:40,524
What's your name?

368
00:40:41,483 --> 00:40:43,652
- André.
- André what?

369
00:40:44,319 --> 00:40:45,988
Those are the people you want.

370
00:40:46,071 --> 00:40:48,699
They're the ones in charge. I can help you
find them.

371
00:40:49,450 --> 00:40:50,784
I don't need your help.

372
00:40:52,286 --> 00:40:54,830
But I'll add these names to my list.

373
00:40:56,373 --> 00:40:57,875
André what?

374
00:40:59,418 --> 00:41:00,711
Lavigne.

375
00:41:02,671 --> 00:41:04,631
You're pretty low on the ladder, André.

376
00:41:06,633 --> 00:41:07,760
There you are.

377
00:41:23,150 --> 00:41:24,443
II THE HIGH PRIESTESS

378
00:41:24,526 --> 00:41:27,362
Today's headlines.

379
00:41:27,446 --> 00:41:30,032
Idealistic London prosecutor Samantha Hodges

380
00:41:30,115 --> 00:41:33,118
was shot last week in broad daylight

381
00:41:33,202 --> 00:41:35,454
following a string of savage attacks

382
00:41:35,537 --> 00:41:38,916
on police officers and court employees.

383
00:41:39,458 --> 00:41:42,836
Her funeral will be held this afternoon.

384
00:41:47,841 --> 00:41:51,303
I met Samantha when I moved to London.

385
00:41:51,386 --> 00:41:53,847
She was a mentor,

386
00:41:54,681 --> 00:41:56,767
a dear friend,

387
00:41:57,392 --> 00:42:03,023
and one of the fiercest defenders of justice
this city has ever seen.

388
00:42:05,692 --> 00:42:07,403
We all know who did this.

389
00:42:09,154 --> 00:42:13,659
Samantha dared to stand up to Semyon Chorney

390
00:42:13,742 --> 00:42:15,452
and hold him accountable.

391
00:42:16,161 --> 00:42:18,622
And for that act of courage,

392
00:42:19,206 --> 00:42:21,041
she lost her life.

393
00:42:24,711 --> 00:42:26,380
The system doesn't work.

394
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:40,602
- I'm sorry about your friend.
- Shit.

395
00:42:41,645 --> 00:42:42,729
I didn't mean to scare you.

396
00:42:42,813 --> 00:42:43,814
Well, you did.

397
00:42:44,815 --> 00:42:46,024
My condolences.

398
00:42:46,608 --> 00:42:48,152
Did you know her well?

399
00:42:49,153 --> 00:42:50,612
I didn't even know her.

400
00:42:51,697 --> 00:42:53,907
Well, thank you for the condolences.

401
00:42:56,118 --> 00:42:57,202
Calypso!

402
00:43:06,378 --> 00:43:08,213
I think this belongs to you.

403
00:43:13,802 --> 00:43:14,970
You're...

404
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:17,639
You're that boy.

405
00:43:19,266 --> 00:43:20,893
But no. You were...

406
00:43:20,976 --> 00:43:22,144
- You were...
- I was.

407
00:43:23,312 --> 00:43:24,730
For three minutes.

408
00:43:24,813 --> 00:43:27,733
It would have been a lot longer if it hadn't
been for you.

409
00:43:27,816 --> 00:43:30,527
They're my grandmother's cards.

410
00:43:30,611 --> 00:43:33,238
I still carry the deck with me.

411
00:43:33,906 --> 00:43:35,491
Why did you give it to me?

412
00:43:36,325 --> 00:43:38,077
I thought you needed it.

413
00:43:39,870 --> 00:43:41,580
Was the card all you had?

414
00:43:41,663 --> 00:43:42,998
How did you find me?

415
00:43:45,626 --> 00:43:48,754
Hunting people is what I do.

416
00:43:49,588 --> 00:43:50,589
Hunting?

417
00:43:51,340 --> 00:43:53,008
Do you know who did this?

418
00:43:54,384 --> 00:43:55,928
Yes.

419
00:43:57,387 --> 00:43:58,514
Will they catch him?

420
00:43:59,306 --> 00:44:00,891
I doubt it.

421
00:44:05,813 --> 00:44:07,815
What would you say if I told you...

422
00:44:09,274 --> 00:44:10,651
that I got him?

423
00:44:13,695 --> 00:44:17,116
CRIME BOSS MURDERED IN PRISON

424
00:44:20,494 --> 00:44:24,331
THE DAILY BUGLE - SEVEN MURDERS: IS THERE A
PATTERN?

425
00:44:26,542 --> 00:44:30,045
Cartel leader poisoned on yacht - Darts cannot
be traced

426
00:44:30,129 --> 00:44:34,049
WHO IS THE HUNTER?

427
00:44:47,813 --> 00:44:49,356
A tiger's fang?

428
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:52,025
I use whatever tools I have at hand.

429
00:44:52,776 --> 00:44:54,778
Why did you do that?

430
00:44:54,862 --> 00:44:57,072
Wasn't he responsible for killing your friend?

431
00:44:59,032 --> 00:45:03,871
Listen, I've been looking for you for a long time.

432
00:45:04,788 --> 00:45:07,458
It's my way of thanking you for saving my life.

433
00:45:07,541 --> 00:45:09,585
I never asked you to kill anyone.

434
00:45:09,668 --> 00:45:11,128
I'm a lawyer.

435
00:45:14,214 --> 00:45:16,717
But that bastard did deserve it.

436
00:45:20,137 --> 00:45:21,972
I know who your father is.

437
00:45:23,682 --> 00:45:25,142
Are you like him?

438
00:45:25,851 --> 00:45:26,810
A gangster?

439
00:45:26,894 --> 00:45:28,020
No.

440
00:45:30,981 --> 00:45:34,818
Ever since I was a child, I watched my father
bring evil into the world.

441
00:45:34,902 --> 00:45:37,488
He had already decided everything.

442
00:45:37,571 --> 00:45:40,324
I was supposed to follow in his footsteps

443
00:45:40,407 --> 00:45:43,118
and take over the family business.

444
00:45:44,161 --> 00:45:46,747
But something happened to me the day you saw me.

445
00:45:49,041 --> 00:45:53,629
So I got as far away from my father as I could.

446
00:45:55,339 --> 00:45:58,258
And now I get rid of men like him.

447
00:45:59,301 --> 00:46:00,636
So you are the Hunter?

448
00:46:01,804 --> 00:46:04,014
That's what the press calls me.

449
00:46:05,891 --> 00:46:07,351
I prefer Kraven.

450
00:46:07,434 --> 00:46:08,769
Kraven?

451
00:46:09,478 --> 00:46:10,562
With a K.

452
00:46:11,772 --> 00:46:14,316
The only people who've heard that name are dead.

453
00:46:15,067 --> 00:46:18,070
Then I'd better be careful.

454
00:46:19,405 --> 00:46:21,156
And you live here?

455
00:46:21,782 --> 00:46:25,411
I couldn't live farther from here.

456
00:46:27,287 --> 00:46:28,831
But my brother does.

457
00:46:30,666 --> 00:46:31,917
And I...

458
00:46:34,878 --> 00:46:39,383
I haven't always been there for him, so I see
him when I can.

459
00:46:41,176 --> 00:46:42,803
What about you?

460
00:46:42,886 --> 00:46:44,721
How did you end up here?

461
00:46:44,805 --> 00:46:46,723
Sometimes I don't know myself.

462
00:46:49,643 --> 00:46:52,896
My parents were lawyers, so that's what I do.

463
00:46:53,856 --> 00:46:56,275
I spent seven years in the New York DA's office

464
00:46:56,358 --> 00:46:58,444
until I couldn't take it anymore.

465
00:46:59,361 --> 00:47:02,156
Sometimes the law gets in the way of justice.

466
00:47:02,698 --> 00:47:04,116
That's true.

467
00:47:05,909 --> 00:47:09,872
So I joined one of Europe's biggest law firms.

468
00:47:10,789 --> 00:47:12,082
I know where you work.

469
00:47:12,166 --> 00:47:15,335
You're one of their best legal investigators.

470
00:47:16,086 --> 00:47:17,546
And I also know...

471
00:47:18,881 --> 00:47:21,800
your clients aren't exactly angels.

472
00:47:21,884 --> 00:47:23,177
That's true.

473
00:47:24,386 --> 00:47:26,972
And what can you accomplish from behind a desk?

474
00:47:29,224 --> 00:47:30,517
I have a list.

475
00:47:31,351 --> 00:47:32,728
A list?

476
00:47:37,274 --> 00:47:40,861
There are other ways to do what you're trying
to do, Calypso.

477
00:47:52,539 --> 00:47:54,583
You'll need a lawyer, or worse,

478
00:47:54,666 --> 00:47:56,418
if you keep going after that world.

479
00:47:59,213 --> 00:48:00,756
How about a partnership?

480
00:48:01,882 --> 00:48:05,135
At the firm, you can find people I can't.

481
00:48:05,219 --> 00:48:07,137
- And that way I could...
- Yeah, I get it.

482
00:48:12,476 --> 00:48:13,602
I'll think about it.

483
00:48:15,062 --> 00:48:16,313
Kraven.

484
00:48:17,064 --> 00:48:19,066
And some advice, as a friend.

485
00:48:19,149 --> 00:48:22,027
If you go after the names on that list,

486
00:48:22,111 --> 00:48:25,322
they'll hurt the people you love.

487
00:48:35,874 --> 00:48:37,709
Hey! Raja!

488
00:48:37,793 --> 00:48:39,420
We need to talk about this.

489
00:48:39,503 --> 00:48:41,713
Yes. Again?

490
00:48:41,797 --> 00:48:42,965
Run, run!

491
00:48:48,470 --> 00:48:49,596
Didn't you hear me?

492
00:48:50,472 --> 00:48:52,057
Raja.

493
00:48:52,141 --> 00:48:54,601
Come here, give it to me.

494
00:48:54,685 --> 00:48:56,812
Oh, you're going to make me beg?

495
00:48:58,856 --> 00:49:00,232
You know I don't beg.

496
00:49:01,483 --> 00:49:03,318
Do you think I'm weak?

497
00:49:05,821 --> 00:49:07,489
Give me that thing.

498
00:49:10,200 --> 00:49:12,035
Raja!

499
00:49:12,119 --> 00:49:14,997
It's okay, Rajinka. Yes.

500
00:49:15,080 --> 00:49:16,915
You're my little Ryazhuchka.

501
00:49:16,999 --> 00:49:19,752
Daddy loves you. Daddy forgives you.

502
00:49:19,835 --> 00:49:21,253
One more thing.

503
00:49:21,879 --> 00:49:24,506
Semyon Chorney was killed in his cell.

504
00:49:26,258 --> 00:49:27,426
Who killed him?

505
00:49:27,509 --> 00:49:29,386
They say it was the Hunter.

506
00:49:30,429 --> 00:49:32,389
Faster than a cheetah,

507
00:49:32,473 --> 00:49:34,308
cunning as a fox.

508
00:49:35,100 --> 00:49:37,603
More ferocious than a tiger.

509
00:49:41,982 --> 00:49:43,233
Tell me,

510
00:49:43,317 --> 00:49:47,404
do you think this Hunter really exists?

511
00:49:47,488 --> 00:49:49,323
It could all be lies.

512
00:49:50,074 --> 00:49:52,076
But they say he has a list.

513
00:49:52,159 --> 00:49:54,036
And if he puts you on it,

514
00:49:54,119 --> 00:49:55,204
he never crosses you off.

515
00:49:57,331 --> 00:49:59,583
And chances are you're on it.

516
00:50:03,003 --> 00:50:04,421
If he exists...

517
00:50:05,297 --> 00:50:06,673
he can be found.

518
00:50:07,633 --> 00:50:08,967
I'll see what I can find out.

519
00:50:10,135 --> 00:50:11,136
Wait.

520
00:50:12,971 --> 00:50:16,350
Chorney's operations are up for grabs, right?

521
00:50:16,433 --> 00:50:17,726
Arrange a meeting.

522
00:50:19,144 --> 00:50:21,230
With his three top men.

523
00:50:44,169 --> 00:50:47,381
Your boss, Semyon Chorney, is dead.

524
00:50:48,215 --> 00:50:52,469
I intend to take over his business dealings.

525
00:50:52,553 --> 00:50:56,473
One of you will be my partner. Which one?

526
00:50:58,308 --> 00:50:59,601
Best offer wins.

527
00:50:59,685 --> 00:51:01,812
He calls himself Rhino.

528
00:51:01,895 --> 00:51:03,230
He doesn't look like a rhinoceros.

529
00:51:03,313 --> 00:51:05,649
But aren't you curious

530
00:51:06,358 --> 00:51:08,485
why they call me Rhino?

531
00:51:15,576 --> 00:51:16,702
Why are you hurting yourself?

532
00:51:18,495 --> 00:51:20,456
You need to see who you're dealing with.

533
00:51:33,093 --> 00:51:34,678
Get rid of him.

534
00:51:41,435 --> 00:51:43,103
It's all right, Raja.

535
00:51:43,645 --> 00:51:45,022
It's all right.

536
00:52:23,519 --> 00:52:25,437
You can lower your weapons.

537
00:52:25,521 --> 00:52:28,190
If I wanted to kill you, all I'd have to do is
raise...

538
00:52:28,273 --> 00:52:29,274
No!

539
00:52:32,027 --> 00:52:36,740
When a rhino sees an opportunity, he doesn't
hesitate.

540
00:52:38,158 --> 00:52:40,077
He charges.

541
00:52:41,412 --> 00:52:43,372
So I'll ask again.

542
00:52:45,124 --> 00:52:47,084
Which one of you is going to be my partner?

543
00:52:53,006 --> 00:52:54,466
Excellent offer.

544
00:52:58,137 --> 00:52:59,263
We have a winner.

545
00:53:48,854 --> 00:53:50,314
My son Dmitri.

546
00:53:51,940 --> 00:53:54,276
The next one's for you, Dad.

547
00:54:01,575 --> 00:54:04,870
He sings it for me. He knows I like Tony Bennett.

548
00:54:04,953 --> 00:54:06,288
Do you like Tony Bennett?

549
00:54:06,830 --> 00:54:09,416
I don't trust anyone who doesn't like Tony
Bennett.

550
00:54:11,794 --> 00:54:14,338
He can imitate anyone. He's like a chameleon.

551
00:54:16,965 --> 00:54:18,467
Those killers...

552
00:54:19,510 --> 00:54:22,387
if they got to your boss in prison,

553
00:54:23,639 --> 00:54:26,350
I think we need to take precautions.

554
00:54:26,433 --> 00:54:27,893
I understand.

555
00:54:27,976 --> 00:54:28,977
Come closer.

556
00:54:31,647 --> 00:54:34,233
Chorney is dead.

557
00:54:35,359 --> 00:54:38,946
That leaves your operations vulnerable.

558
00:54:40,656 --> 00:54:42,616
I can offer you security,

559
00:54:43,158 --> 00:54:46,161
distribution, and most importantly,

560
00:54:46,245 --> 00:54:47,830
peace and quiet.

561
00:54:48,497 --> 00:54:51,083
Sounds good. Deal.

562
00:54:52,376 --> 00:54:53,836
Just like that?

563
00:54:54,670 --> 00:54:58,173
- Don't you want to think it over?
- Order needs to be restored.

564
00:54:58,715 --> 00:54:59,883
The sooner, the better.

565
00:55:02,970 --> 00:55:06,682
You've already made another deal, haven't you?

566
00:55:06,765 --> 00:55:08,100
With whom?

567
00:55:08,183 --> 00:55:10,060
Rhino sends his regards.

568
00:55:42,509 --> 00:55:43,510
Get up.

569
00:56:01,445 --> 00:56:02,571
You got shot.

570
00:56:03,822 --> 00:56:05,449
Are you okay, Dad?

571
00:56:11,663 --> 00:56:14,291
Look what they've done to my club.

572
00:56:17,127 --> 00:56:18,837
They attack me

573
00:56:18,921 --> 00:56:20,923
on my own turf.

574
00:56:22,424 --> 00:56:25,094
And who do I have to defend me?

575
00:56:25,177 --> 00:56:26,845
My son,

576
00:56:26,929 --> 00:56:28,597
the piano player.

577
00:56:29,556 --> 00:56:31,642
Come on! Hit me!

578
00:56:31,725 --> 00:56:32,935
Fight!

579
00:56:34,061 --> 00:56:35,604
I need fighters,

580
00:56:35,687 --> 00:56:37,398
not a coward.

581
00:56:38,357 --> 00:56:40,651
You can't even defend yourself.

582
00:56:46,990 --> 00:56:48,867
The hit on Kravinoff failed.

583
00:56:49,451 --> 00:56:51,203
Our men are dead.

584
00:57:01,630 --> 00:57:04,007
Nikolai is one tough old bear.

585
00:57:04,091 --> 00:57:06,301
He won't go down without a fight.

586
00:57:08,429 --> 00:57:10,597
Someone slipped this under my door.

587
00:57:21,775 --> 00:57:22,776
MATCH: 97.3%

588
00:57:22,860 --> 00:57:23,944
SERGEI KRAVINOFF - VOLGOGRAD, RUSSIA

589
00:57:24,027 --> 00:57:25,112
FATHER: NIKOLAI KRAVINOFF - MOTHER: DECEASED
(SUICIDE)

590
00:57:25,195 --> 00:57:26,280
ALIAS: KRAVEN THE HUNTER

591
00:57:26,363 --> 00:57:30,659
Nikolai Kravinoff's son Sergei is the Hunter?

592
00:57:30,743 --> 00:57:33,871
But what's this Kraven thing?

593
00:57:33,954 --> 00:57:36,290
Apparently, that's what he calls himself.

594
00:57:36,832 --> 00:57:38,625
That can't be real.

595
00:57:40,919 --> 00:57:43,464
- Can it?
- I don't know.

596
00:57:44,089 --> 00:57:46,175
Give it to the Foreigner.

597
00:57:46,258 --> 00:57:48,177
He's a fucking weirdo,

598
00:57:48,260 --> 00:57:50,971
but he's been obsessed with the Hunter for years.

599
00:57:51,597 --> 00:57:54,767
Let's see if he can figure out what the hell
is going on.

600
00:58:07,863 --> 00:58:08,697
Hey!

601
00:58:08,781 --> 00:58:10,574
What are you doing?

602
00:58:10,657 --> 00:58:12,076
It's okay.

603
00:58:12,159 --> 00:58:14,912
I'm looking for the prisoner who killed Semyon
Chorney.

604
00:58:16,538 --> 00:58:17,998
Turn around.

605
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:21,168
Turn around.

606
00:58:23,420 --> 00:58:25,214
You are not allowed in here!

607
00:58:25,297 --> 00:58:28,300
They call me the Foreigner because I don't
belong anywhere.

608
00:58:35,641 --> 00:58:36,642
One.

609
00:58:39,019 --> 00:58:40,020
Two.

610
00:58:42,606 --> 00:58:43,816
Three.

611
00:59:04,628 --> 00:59:06,004
See you later.

612
00:59:25,566 --> 00:59:27,693
This is amazing. Does it have a river view?

613
01:00:23,373 --> 01:00:24,875
Surprise!

614
01:00:24,958 --> 01:00:26,085
You idiot!

615
01:00:26,168 --> 01:00:27,336
Sergei!

616
01:00:30,172 --> 01:00:32,382
You scared the shit out of me!

617
01:00:33,217 --> 01:00:35,636
Happy birthday, little brother.

618
01:00:37,137 --> 01:00:38,639
I love you!

619
01:00:40,849 --> 01:00:42,726
What are we going to do, huh?

620
01:00:44,103 --> 01:00:45,270
You're not going out dressed like that.

621
01:00:45,354 --> 01:00:47,439
- Great, we're staying here.
- What?

622
01:00:47,523 --> 01:00:48,982
It's my birthday.

623
01:00:49,525 --> 01:00:51,985
On your birthday, we can go

624
01:00:52,569 --> 01:00:54,822
pet some animals

625
01:00:54,905 --> 01:00:56,907
or wherever you have fun.

626
01:00:56,990 --> 01:01:00,285
But tonight, this.

627
01:01:02,538 --> 01:01:04,081
You think it'll fit me?

628
01:01:04,164 --> 01:01:07,126
It's huge on me. It'll fit you perfectly.

629
01:01:10,337 --> 01:01:11,422
- Sorry.
- Thank you.

630
01:01:11,505 --> 01:01:12,756
You're welcome.

631
01:01:12,840 --> 01:01:14,466
Nice cologne, by the way.

632
01:01:14,550 --> 01:01:15,968
Thanks, but I'm not wearing any.

633
01:01:21,014 --> 01:01:22,808
I knew he'd find out about you eventually.

634
01:01:26,979 --> 01:01:29,231
Dad was sitting right here.

635
01:01:29,314 --> 01:01:31,608
It all happened so fast.

636
01:01:31,692 --> 01:01:35,195
You find out who you are in moments like that.

637
01:01:35,279 --> 01:01:36,405
And I'm a coward.

638
01:01:36,488 --> 01:01:39,658
Dima, you're not a coward. It's natural to be
afraid.

639
01:01:39,742 --> 01:01:40,993
That's your instincts talking.

640
01:01:41,076 --> 01:01:43,829
Why don't we get to choose who we are?

641
01:01:43,912 --> 01:01:45,122
Why do I have to be me?

642
01:01:45,205 --> 01:01:47,499
I have to be strong, fearless.

643
01:01:47,583 --> 01:01:50,544
Run toward bullets instead of collapsing on
the floor.

644
01:01:50,627 --> 01:01:52,463
Why do you want to be someone else?

645
01:01:52,546 --> 01:01:54,298
So he'll respect me!

646
01:01:54,381 --> 01:01:57,384
Dad's a criminal. What good is his respect?

647
01:01:57,468 --> 01:02:00,929
You act like you don't care, like you're above it.

648
01:02:01,013 --> 01:02:03,182
- Like he can't touch you.
- He can't.

649
01:02:03,265 --> 01:02:06,226
He made you hate people.

650
01:02:06,310 --> 01:02:07,686
I don't hate people.

651
01:02:09,188 --> 01:02:10,814
I hate what people do.

652
01:02:10,898 --> 01:02:12,649
But I don't hate people.

653
01:02:14,276 --> 01:02:15,527
I think...

654
01:02:16,278 --> 01:02:18,405
Dad was right about one thing.

655
01:02:18,489 --> 01:02:20,282
Yeah? What?

656
01:02:21,366 --> 01:02:25,245
Man should be the only animal that poses a threat.

657
01:02:25,329 --> 01:02:27,498
I'm glad I didn't miss the party.

658
01:02:28,499 --> 01:02:30,959
- How could I not come...
- Dad!

659
01:02:31,043 --> 01:02:33,545
...and miss the chance to see both my sons?

660
01:02:35,297 --> 01:02:36,298
Dmitri.

661
01:02:38,258 --> 01:02:39,301
For you.

662
01:02:43,889 --> 01:02:47,101
I don't expect a hug, but not even a handshake?

663
01:02:54,108 --> 01:02:55,109
Dasha.

664
01:03:00,280 --> 01:03:02,616
I only came to make a toast

665
01:03:03,158 --> 01:03:04,618
in honor of Dmitri

666
01:03:05,327 --> 01:03:07,037
on his big day.

667
01:03:08,163 --> 01:03:09,164
Pour.

668
01:03:13,419 --> 01:03:16,964
Pour for men, not boys.

669
01:03:24,179 --> 01:03:25,431
Cheers, Sergei.

670
01:03:28,976 --> 01:03:30,477
To the Kravinoffs.

671
01:03:31,937 --> 01:03:35,816
May we learn to forget the past

672
01:03:36,817 --> 01:03:38,193
and imagine a future

673
01:03:38,277 --> 01:03:39,528
together,

674
01:03:40,529 --> 01:03:41,905
as a family.

675
01:03:49,413 --> 01:03:51,039
That's it.

676
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:54,001
You okay?

677
01:03:58,589 --> 01:03:59,715
Sergei.

678
01:04:02,384 --> 01:04:05,596
I know why you come every year.

679
01:04:06,722 --> 01:04:07,723
Because you feel...

680
01:04:08,474 --> 01:04:10,184
guilty

681
01:04:10,267 --> 01:04:13,937
about leaving me with him.

682
01:04:14,021 --> 01:04:16,398
And I forgive you...

683
01:04:18,108 --> 01:04:19,109
for...

684
01:04:20,694 --> 01:04:21,695
everything.

685
01:04:27,159 --> 01:04:28,410
I'm sorry.

686
01:04:42,716 --> 01:04:45,636
Sergei! Sergei!

687
01:05:14,790 --> 01:05:16,250
You two never want anything, do you?

688
01:05:17,167 --> 01:05:18,460
Can you hold the elevator?

689
01:05:19,086 --> 01:05:20,921
Please? Buddy?

690
01:05:27,302 --> 01:05:28,929
Penthouse, please.

691
01:05:34,309 --> 01:05:35,394
I tried to stop it.

692
01:05:35,477 --> 01:05:36,520
No, you didn't.

693
01:05:38,772 --> 01:05:39,898
This?

694
01:05:39,982 --> 01:05:42,568
It's my travel knife. It's for work.

695
01:05:44,862 --> 01:05:47,197
What exactly do you do for work?

696
01:05:47,281 --> 01:05:48,699
I hunt...

697
01:05:51,869 --> 01:05:53,120
people.

698
01:05:59,835 --> 01:06:00,836
Dmitri?

699
01:06:08,969 --> 01:06:10,888
No, please! Let me go!

700
01:06:37,664 --> 01:06:39,416
Wait, wait! Please!

701
01:06:39,500 --> 01:06:41,835
Wait! We can work this out.

702
01:06:41,919 --> 01:06:43,253
Put him to sleep now.

703
01:07:01,563 --> 01:07:02,564
There he is!

704
01:07:03,607 --> 01:07:04,441
Lose him!

705
01:07:05,859 --> 01:07:07,694
Get out of the fucking way!

706
01:07:09,154 --> 01:07:09,988
Look out!

707
01:07:33,220 --> 01:07:34,138
Shit!

708
01:07:35,514 --> 01:07:36,723
Step on it!

709
01:07:41,562 --> 01:07:42,396
Faster!

710
01:08:08,630 --> 01:08:10,132
Dmitri!

711
01:08:14,595 --> 01:08:17,055
It's armored inside and out, idiot!

712
01:08:25,564 --> 01:08:26,732
Get him off there!

713
01:09:36,427 --> 01:09:37,511
Come on! Come on!

714
01:10:22,389 --> 01:10:24,433
Dima!

715
01:10:27,311 --> 01:10:29,104
Hello, sir. Can I help you?

716
01:10:29,188 --> 01:10:30,647
Perhaps a towel?

717
01:10:31,648 --> 01:10:34,234
Thank you very much. Really.

718
01:10:40,407 --> 01:10:41,241
Sir.

719
01:10:41,867 --> 01:10:43,452
You left your shoes downstairs.

720
01:10:43,535 --> 01:10:45,537
- I didn't forget anything.
- Why don't we go

721
01:10:45,621 --> 01:10:48,123
- look for them?
- Not enough volts.

722
01:10:48,707 --> 01:10:51,585
Brian! It's okay. He's a client.

723
01:10:52,211 --> 01:10:54,004
What's wrong with you, Sergei?

724
01:10:54,088 --> 01:10:56,423
I told you I'd think about your offer.

725
01:10:56,507 --> 01:10:58,634
You can't just show up like this.

726
01:10:58,717 --> 01:10:59,968
This is where I work.

727
01:11:00,052 --> 01:11:01,345
They have my brother.

728
01:11:01,887 --> 01:11:02,971
Who has him?

729
01:11:03,055 --> 01:11:04,306
There were four men.

730
01:11:05,307 --> 01:11:06,725
They took him from his home.

731
01:11:07,309 --> 01:11:09,728
- Did you see them?
- One of them had...

732
01:11:10,813 --> 01:11:13,941
dark hair, brown eyes, a scar below his left eye.

733
01:11:14,024 --> 01:11:15,317
A Turkish accent.

734
01:11:15,401 --> 01:11:16,568
Shit.

735
01:11:16,652 --> 01:11:19,488
- You talked to them.
- Not exactly.

736
01:11:20,614 --> 01:11:23,492
But there was a lot of shouting.

737
01:11:27,287 --> 01:11:28,288
Okay.

738
01:11:29,748 --> 01:11:31,291
We need to find him.

739
01:11:33,419 --> 01:11:35,546
I should've been there with him.

740
01:11:36,755 --> 01:11:38,507
I couldn't sleep, so...

741
01:11:39,675 --> 01:11:41,802
I left. I went for a walk and...

742
01:11:41,885 --> 01:11:43,220
We'll find him.

743
01:11:45,055 --> 01:11:46,056
Okay?

744
01:11:46,932 --> 01:11:48,350
I'll do what I do best.

745
01:11:48,434 --> 01:11:50,102
I'll get you a name.

746
01:11:51,103 --> 01:11:54,314
Then you'll do what you do best.

747
01:11:55,315 --> 01:11:57,192
And we'll get him back.

748
01:11:58,736 --> 01:12:02,072
I'm looking for a mercenary who kidnapped
someone in London.

749
01:12:02,156 --> 01:12:04,491
He has a scar under his eye.

750
01:12:04,575 --> 01:12:07,369
He smokes Turkish cigarettes. I assume he's
from there.

751
01:12:08,078 --> 01:12:09,705
Find him.

752
01:12:13,292 --> 01:12:14,501
Sergei.

753
01:12:14,585 --> 01:12:16,086
Who are they?

754
01:12:16,170 --> 01:12:17,880
They didn't tell me.

755
01:12:17,963 --> 01:12:19,631
But you know, don't you?

756
01:12:19,715 --> 01:12:22,342
My list of enemies is long.

757
01:12:26,180 --> 01:12:28,015
Look what they did to him.

758
01:12:39,318 --> 01:12:40,486
How much do they want?

759
01:12:41,695 --> 01:12:43,072
Twenty million.

760
01:12:43,697 --> 01:12:45,324
In 48 hours.

761
01:12:49,453 --> 01:12:50,537
Pay them.

762
01:12:51,455 --> 01:12:52,539
It's complicated.

763
01:12:52,623 --> 01:12:55,000
No, it's not. It's very simple.

764
01:12:55,709 --> 01:12:58,253
You have the money, and he's your son.

765
01:12:58,337 --> 01:13:00,172
This isn't about money.

766
01:13:00,255 --> 01:13:02,382
It's about power.

767
01:13:05,511 --> 01:13:06,887
If I pay them,

768
01:13:07,429 --> 01:13:08,847
I'm weak.

769
01:13:09,473 --> 01:13:11,183
If I show weakness,

770
01:13:11,266 --> 01:13:15,187
I lose everything I've spent my life building.

771
01:13:15,270 --> 01:13:17,648
Spent your life building what?

772
01:13:18,565 --> 01:13:20,234
You're a drug dealer.

773
01:13:24,863 --> 01:13:26,782
You don't get to hit me anymore.

774
01:13:27,783 --> 01:13:29,576
Dmitri is innocent.

775
01:13:29,660 --> 01:13:33,122
If you let them kill him, his blood will be on
your hands.

776
01:13:33,205 --> 01:13:34,623
On my hands?

777
01:13:35,165 --> 01:13:36,583
Mine?

778
01:13:36,667 --> 01:13:38,752
I'm not the one who abandoned him.

779
01:13:39,670 --> 01:13:42,047
You abandoned him.

780
01:13:43,590 --> 01:13:44,633
You.

781
01:13:47,970 --> 01:13:50,431
He was dead the moment they kidnapped him!

782
01:13:51,181 --> 01:13:53,225
Whether I pay them or not!

783
01:13:55,060 --> 01:13:56,186
You don't...

784
01:13:56,270 --> 01:13:57,563
You don't know that.

785
01:13:57,646 --> 01:13:59,982
Yes, I do.

786
01:14:01,275 --> 01:14:03,360
Because that's what I would do.

787
01:14:03,944 --> 01:14:05,779
You're disgusting.

788
01:14:05,863 --> 01:14:07,698
Of course I want him back.

789
01:14:08,991 --> 01:14:11,618
I want both my sons back.

790
01:14:19,001 --> 01:14:21,462
Some legend you've become.

791
01:14:25,132 --> 01:14:26,133
Wake up!

792
01:14:28,677 --> 01:14:29,970
Drink this.

793
01:14:30,554 --> 01:14:31,764
Antibiotics.

794
01:14:31,847 --> 01:14:34,099
I can't let you die, can I?

795
01:14:43,859 --> 01:14:46,195
"I can't let you die, can I?"

796
01:14:52,618 --> 01:14:53,911
All right.

797
01:15:22,940 --> 01:15:24,441
Ömer Ozdemir.

798
01:15:25,234 --> 01:15:28,529
He's hiding in a monastery outside Ankara.

799
01:15:29,154 --> 01:15:30,322
Thank you.

800
01:15:30,406 --> 01:15:32,950
Thank me by never calling me again.

801
01:15:33,033 --> 01:15:34,118
We'll see.

802
01:15:42,251 --> 01:15:43,585
How did it go?

803
01:15:46,755 --> 01:15:49,508
- She took it.
- Of course she did.

804
01:15:49,591 --> 01:15:50,926
But did she believe you?

805
01:15:51,009 --> 01:15:53,178
Yes. She trusts me.

806
01:15:54,930 --> 01:15:57,683
That's why I want twice what your boss promised.

807
01:15:58,225 --> 01:15:59,309
Twice?

808
01:16:00,227 --> 01:16:01,937
Wouldn't you prefer three times as much?

809
01:16:02,020 --> 01:16:03,647
Are you kidding?

810
01:16:07,234 --> 01:16:08,318
One.

811
01:16:10,738 --> 01:16:11,780
Two.

812
01:16:12,656 --> 01:16:13,490
Three.

813
01:16:16,368 --> 01:16:17,369
Done.

814
01:16:29,214 --> 01:16:30,591
Get ready.

815
01:16:31,341 --> 01:16:34,428
The Hunter is on his way.

816
01:16:35,387 --> 01:16:39,141
Sergei. The man you're looking for is Ömer
Ozdemir.

817
01:16:39,933 --> 01:16:43,604
I found a monastery registered to his family
in Turkey.

818
01:16:43,687 --> 01:16:46,565
And that's where your brother is.

819
01:16:47,608 --> 01:16:48,859
I appreciate it.

820
01:16:50,069 --> 01:16:52,154
All set, Ellie! Let's go!

821
01:16:53,363 --> 01:16:56,825
NORTHERN TURKEY

822
01:17:34,154 --> 01:17:35,364
Okay.

823
01:18:58,113 --> 01:18:59,323
That's him.

824
01:19:19,968 --> 01:19:21,011
He's here.

825
01:19:28,102 --> 01:19:29,561
Where's Dmitri?

826
01:19:34,358 --> 01:19:35,359
Where is he?

827
01:19:36,360 --> 01:19:39,488
Let me go, or you'll never see your brother
again...

828
01:19:40,072 --> 01:19:41,073
Kraven.

829
01:20:06,807 --> 01:20:08,392
How do you know my name?

830
01:20:08,475 --> 01:20:09,935
Who set me up?

831
01:20:10,018 --> 01:20:11,895
Who has my brother?

832
01:20:13,063 --> 01:20:14,523
Rhino.

833
01:20:14,606 --> 01:20:16,275
He's already killed us both.

834
01:20:40,549 --> 01:20:41,383
Hey!

835
01:20:41,467 --> 01:20:42,885
Who are you?

836
01:20:42,968 --> 01:20:45,220
Does anyone have an evidence bag?

837
01:20:45,304 --> 01:20:47,139
I left mine in the car.

838
01:20:47,222 --> 01:20:48,348
What are you saying?

839
01:20:49,266 --> 01:20:52,352
This is ground rosary pea.

840
01:20:53,771 --> 01:20:55,856
Whoever did this knows about toxins.

841
01:20:58,358 --> 01:20:59,318
One.

842
01:21:01,236 --> 01:21:02,154
Two.

843
01:21:04,364 --> 01:21:05,449
Three.

844
01:21:08,619 --> 01:21:09,787
What are you doing?

845
01:21:14,249 --> 01:21:15,542
See you later.

846
01:21:22,466 --> 01:21:23,801
That's enough, Raja.

847
01:21:25,260 --> 01:21:27,429
I'm sorry about your finger.

848
01:21:27,513 --> 01:21:29,264
It was collateral damage.

849
01:21:29,348 --> 01:21:30,724
Let him go.

850
01:21:36,355 --> 01:21:37,731
We met once...

851
01:21:38,774 --> 01:21:40,734
on a hunting trip with your father.

852
01:21:40,818 --> 01:21:43,195
I don't remember.

853
01:21:43,862 --> 01:21:47,241
I suppose not. My hair was different.

854
01:21:47,324 --> 01:21:49,034
And you were very young.

855
01:21:49,118 --> 01:21:50,244
Me?

856
01:21:52,413 --> 01:21:54,039
I've never forgotten it.

857
01:21:56,625 --> 01:21:58,710
And you haven't spoken to my father?

858
01:21:59,503 --> 01:22:02,297
He still won't agree to pay you?

859
01:22:02,381 --> 01:22:03,757
No.

860
01:22:03,841 --> 01:22:07,136
Nikolai Kravinoff would never pay twenty million

861
01:22:07,219 --> 01:22:09,179
to get his bastard son back.

862
01:22:11,181 --> 01:22:14,101
You were an accident, Dmitri.

863
01:22:15,602 --> 01:22:18,522
You came into this world by accident,

864
01:22:18,605 --> 01:22:21,775
and you fell into my hands by accident.

865
01:22:22,818 --> 01:22:23,986
So you're letting me go?

866
01:22:24,069 --> 01:22:25,863
The men who kidnapped you

867
01:22:25,946 --> 01:22:28,282
weren't after you.

868
01:22:28,365 --> 01:22:30,325
They were after your brother.

869
01:22:30,409 --> 01:22:31,618
Sergei?

870
01:22:31,702 --> 01:22:33,579
You both went inside,

871
01:22:33,662 --> 01:22:36,123
but when my men went upstairs... Poof!

872
01:22:36,206 --> 01:22:37,875
He vanished.

873
01:22:37,958 --> 01:22:39,626
Like he always does.

874
01:22:40,586 --> 01:22:42,421
So they brought you instead.

875
01:22:42,504 --> 01:22:43,756
Lucky me.

876
01:22:43,839 --> 01:22:46,550
And why do you want Sergei?

877
01:22:46,633 --> 01:22:49,678
- He's never hurt anyone.
- So you don't know, huh?

878
01:22:49,762 --> 01:22:51,013
Don't know what?

879
01:22:56,852 --> 01:22:58,520
Wait for the ending.

880
01:22:58,604 --> 01:23:00,189
It's the best part.

881
01:23:09,156 --> 01:23:12,201
ALIAS: KRAVEN THE HUNTER

882
01:23:12,284 --> 01:23:13,285
Kraven?

883
01:23:13,368 --> 01:23:16,163
Apparently that's what he calls himself.

884
01:23:16,997 --> 01:23:19,666
You think my brother Sergei is the Hunter?

885
01:23:19,750 --> 01:23:21,585
The Hunter is a story.

886
01:23:21,668 --> 01:23:23,921
A fable to frighten criminals.

887
01:23:24,004 --> 01:23:27,091
Clearly, you didn't know your brother very well.

888
01:23:27,174 --> 01:23:28,592
What do you mean, "didn't know"?

889
01:23:28,675 --> 01:23:30,219
Kraven had a list.

890
01:23:30,969 --> 01:23:33,138
If he put you on it, he never crossed you off.

891
01:23:40,771 --> 01:23:42,940
So I killed him first.

892
01:23:53,367 --> 01:23:54,827
I'm going to record this.

893
01:23:57,162 --> 01:23:59,373
We killed Kraven.

894
01:24:01,959 --> 01:24:03,669
Don't celebrate just yet.

895
01:24:18,225 --> 01:24:19,768
- Hello?
- Calypso, it's me.

896
01:24:19,852 --> 01:24:21,770
It was all a trap. Rhino

897
01:24:21,854 --> 01:24:24,314
knows who I am. Now he'll come after you.

898
01:24:24,398 --> 01:24:26,024
Sergei, what are you...?

899
01:24:26,108 --> 01:24:27,067
Shit!

900
01:24:27,151 --> 01:24:31,447
There are five guys in my building who don't
look like they belong here.

901
01:24:31,530 --> 01:24:33,031
You need to leave. Now.

902
01:24:33,115 --> 01:24:35,117
Go to Stansted Airport.

903
01:24:35,200 --> 01:24:36,952
I'll send someone for you.

904
01:25:04,271 --> 01:25:06,523
This is my feeding pack.

905
01:25:08,317 --> 01:25:12,321
It's a mixture of drugs to manage my condition.

906
01:25:13,363 --> 01:25:14,698
What happened to you?

907
01:25:14,782 --> 01:25:16,950
I was underestimated, too.

908
01:25:17,701 --> 01:25:21,413
I was in and out of hospitals, and they never
knew what was wrong with me.

909
01:25:21,497 --> 01:25:25,250
I knew I'd never earn your father's respect...

910
01:25:26,418 --> 01:25:27,961
or anyone else's...

911
01:25:29,129 --> 01:25:31,298
until I became strong.

912
01:25:31,882 --> 01:25:34,009
I tried everything.

913
01:25:34,093 --> 01:25:35,552
And then...

914
01:25:37,513 --> 01:25:39,098
I found someone.

915
01:25:39,973 --> 01:25:41,308
In New York,

916
01:25:42,476 --> 01:25:44,019
a biochemist,

917
01:25:44,103 --> 01:25:46,772
a professor named Miles Warren.

918
01:25:46,855 --> 01:25:52,152
He was developing a procedure to increase strength

919
01:25:52,736 --> 01:25:54,196
tenfold.

920
01:25:56,156 --> 01:25:58,367
And I signed up on the spot.

921
01:26:04,206 --> 01:26:07,251
My skin began to harden.

922
01:26:07,334 --> 01:26:08,794
It was...

923
01:26:09,753 --> 01:26:11,422
indestructible,

924
01:26:12,256 --> 01:26:14,383
like a rhinoceros.

925
01:26:15,717 --> 01:26:17,886
But the pain...

926
01:26:20,681 --> 01:26:21,932
was too much.

927
01:26:41,827 --> 01:26:46,039
I think we all have an animal inside us, Dmitri.

928
01:26:47,916 --> 01:26:50,419
I'm going to take your father's territory.

929
01:26:50,502 --> 01:26:52,755
I want you to partner with me.

930
01:26:53,714 --> 01:26:56,425
The Kravinoff name will still open doors,

931
01:26:56,508 --> 01:26:59,470
and you'll finally get the respect you deserve.

932
01:27:00,846 --> 01:27:02,306
You're right.

933
01:27:03,891 --> 01:27:06,226
I have been underestimated

934
01:27:07,644 --> 01:27:09,021
my whole life.

935
01:27:14,568 --> 01:27:17,071
But if you think I'll betray my family,

936
01:27:18,697 --> 01:27:20,115
you're wrong.

937
01:27:28,624 --> 01:27:29,458
Boss.

938
01:27:30,459 --> 01:27:33,420
The men haven't checked in. They're not answering.

939
01:27:38,842 --> 01:27:40,761
Kraven's alive.

940
01:27:40,844 --> 01:27:42,012
Hey, Bert!

941
01:27:44,098 --> 01:27:45,599
Alpha Team, Bravo Team.

942
01:27:47,976 --> 01:27:49,228
He's here.

943
01:28:34,773 --> 01:28:35,858
How cute.

944
01:28:36,442 --> 01:28:40,404
Will your trick still work if I gouge your
eyes out?

945
01:28:41,613 --> 01:28:43,240
Relax.

946
01:28:55,711 --> 01:28:58,046
I'm sorry I dragged you into this.

947
01:28:58,130 --> 01:29:00,632
- Any news about Dmitri?
- Not yet.

948
01:29:00,716 --> 01:29:04,970
Three of my sources disappeared while tracking
Rhino's plane.

949
01:29:05,554 --> 01:29:08,640
I don't like where this is going.

950
01:29:10,058 --> 01:29:12,186
What is this place?

951
01:29:12,269 --> 01:29:14,480
The land belonged to my mother's family.

952
01:29:15,814 --> 01:29:19,068
It's all I have left of her.

953
01:29:23,614 --> 01:29:25,032
What's wrong now?

954
01:29:25,699 --> 01:29:27,493
We're being hunted.

955
01:29:28,368 --> 01:29:29,453
By whom?

956
01:29:52,810 --> 01:29:54,853
You don't get to hunt me!

957
01:29:54,937 --> 01:29:56,230
That's right, get angry.

958
01:29:56,313 --> 01:29:58,482
What are you going to do? Come on, show me!

959
01:30:08,033 --> 01:30:10,786
I've seen her since she was a cub,

960
01:30:10,869 --> 01:30:12,913
but I don't remember her being that big.

961
01:30:13,622 --> 01:30:16,333
You're a fucking lunatic. I swear.

962
01:30:16,417 --> 01:30:18,127
You're only just realizing that?

963
01:30:19,503 --> 01:30:21,922
I know I hired you for the job.

964
01:30:23,382 --> 01:30:27,010
But why do you want Kraven? Why the obsession?

965
01:30:27,094 --> 01:30:30,139
My mentor was one of the greatest assassins
who ever lived.

966
01:30:30,222 --> 01:30:32,349
He taught me everything I know.

967
01:30:32,433 --> 01:30:35,811
He was like a brother to me. Maybe you knew him.

968
01:30:37,062 --> 01:30:38,188
I heard of him.

969
01:30:38,272 --> 01:30:40,274
THE DAILY BUGLE - HUNTER VERSUS ASSASSIN

970
01:30:41,108 --> 01:30:42,693
He was killed.

971
01:30:42,776 --> 01:30:46,196
One man got in and slit his throat.

972
01:30:46,280 --> 01:30:47,656
Kraven?

973
01:30:49,241 --> 01:30:50,868
So I've traveled the world,

974
01:30:51,869 --> 01:30:54,121
following him wherever he goes.

975
01:30:54,204 --> 01:30:56,623
But Kraven is the perfect predator.

976
01:30:57,583 --> 01:30:59,543
He has no weaknesses.

977
01:31:02,838 --> 01:31:04,423
But you've found one.

978
01:31:06,133 --> 01:31:07,885
And I know how to exploit it.

979
01:31:07,968 --> 01:31:10,637
Skip to the part I'm interested in.

980
01:31:13,682 --> 01:31:16,685
This is Siberian rosary pea.

981
01:31:16,769 --> 01:31:18,395
A rare species.

982
01:31:19,146 --> 01:31:21,648
I found traces of it in a poison at the monastery.

983
01:31:22,316 --> 01:31:26,153
These peas are native to a specific region of
Siberia.

984
01:31:27,821 --> 01:31:29,490
That's where we'll find him.

985
01:32:01,146 --> 01:32:02,314
Be careful with that.

986
01:32:03,690 --> 01:32:06,026
Actually, I'm very good with these things.

987
01:32:06,777 --> 01:32:09,154
Summer archery classes.

988
01:32:11,949 --> 01:32:13,784
Figwort.

989
01:32:14,660 --> 01:32:16,912
Wild oats.

990
01:32:16,995 --> 01:32:18,622
Tribulus.

991
01:32:21,166 --> 01:32:22,960
Rosary pea?

992
01:32:23,043 --> 01:32:24,837
You know your herbs.

993
01:32:25,754 --> 01:32:26,880
These can kill.

994
01:32:26,964 --> 01:32:28,674
Or save lives.

995
01:32:28,757 --> 01:32:30,551
Nature is funny that way.

996
01:32:31,510 --> 01:32:33,262
What are you trying to do here?

997
01:32:36,807 --> 01:32:38,600
Tell me about this.

998
01:32:39,810 --> 01:32:41,353
It was my grandmother's.

999
01:32:42,354 --> 01:32:44,732
We were on safari and went to visit her that day.

1000
01:32:44,815 --> 01:32:48,777
I've spent years trying to figure out what's
in it.

1001
01:32:49,319 --> 01:32:51,613
My grandmother was some kind of...

1002
01:32:52,239 --> 01:32:53,407
mystic.

1003
01:32:54,199 --> 01:32:56,326
She had all sorts of crazy things.

1004
01:32:57,119 --> 01:33:01,707
My parents never talked about it, but she was
a very powerful woman.

1005
01:33:03,083 --> 01:33:05,586
She said it could heal anyone who drank it...

1006
01:33:06,712 --> 01:33:09,631
in unimaginable ways.

1007
01:33:09,715 --> 01:33:11,884
I was a child.

1008
01:33:11,967 --> 01:33:14,261
I had no idea what it would do.

1009
01:33:14,344 --> 01:33:16,430
This saved my life.

1010
01:33:16,513 --> 01:33:17,556
Really?

1011
01:33:17,639 --> 01:33:19,099
Believe me. It changed me.

1012
01:33:19,183 --> 01:33:20,392
Exactly.

1013
01:33:21,393 --> 01:33:23,020
Look what you've become.

1014
01:33:26,732 --> 01:33:28,150
I need to know

1015
01:33:28,734 --> 01:33:30,402
what was in it.

1016
01:33:32,362 --> 01:33:33,989
And whether you can get more.

1017
01:33:34,656 --> 01:33:35,741
No.

1018
01:33:37,910 --> 01:33:40,996
She died shortly after that trip, and I never
saw her again.

1019
01:33:48,670 --> 01:33:52,257
One of my sources got back to me. Rhino is on
the move.

1020
01:33:52,341 --> 01:33:54,426
We'll know more very soon.

1021
01:33:54,510 --> 01:33:56,220
I knew you'd be good at this.

1022
01:33:59,139 --> 01:34:00,641
Sergei.

1023
01:34:00,724 --> 01:34:02,851
We'll get Dmitri back.

1024
01:34:03,435 --> 01:34:06,021
But is all this worth it?

1025
01:34:06,105 --> 01:34:09,608
Calypso, I was born to do this.

1026
01:34:10,442 --> 01:34:13,404
I'm the greatest hunter on the planet. You
can't deny it.

1027
01:34:14,154 --> 01:34:16,573
I can track or defeat anyone.

1028
01:34:16,657 --> 01:34:19,159
They can't even touch me. So, no.

1029
01:34:19,785 --> 01:34:21,120
Why would I want to stop?

1030
01:34:21,203 --> 01:34:23,622
It's called karma. And it always catches up
with you.

1031
01:34:24,832 --> 01:34:26,333
Not me.

1032
01:34:26,417 --> 01:34:27,960
I'm faster than it.

1033
01:34:31,964 --> 01:34:33,715
But Dmitri wasn't.

1034
01:34:44,017 --> 01:34:46,103
Interesting piece.

1035
01:34:46,186 --> 01:34:48,605
It takes more than a gun to stop Kraven.

1036
01:34:48,689 --> 01:34:52,901
This formula developed by MI6 is highly effective.

1037
01:34:53,652 --> 01:34:54,862
May I?

1038
01:35:00,159 --> 01:35:02,661
First, it unleashes your worst nightmare,

1039
01:35:02,745 --> 01:35:04,788
then paralyzes your vital organs

1040
01:35:04,872 --> 01:35:07,291
before a very violent death.

1041
01:35:09,209 --> 01:35:11,003
I like your style.

1042
01:35:21,930 --> 01:35:24,266
Only one person has this number.

1043
01:35:25,225 --> 01:35:27,144
- Dima, where are you?
- Sergei.

1044
01:35:27,895 --> 01:35:29,897
Sorry, they made me call you.

1045
01:35:29,980 --> 01:35:32,399
- Dmitri.
- I'm afraid not.

1046
01:35:32,483 --> 01:35:34,526
But now you've seen he's alive.

1047
01:35:34,610 --> 01:35:35,819
What do you want?

1048
01:35:35,903 --> 01:35:39,114
My life, without having to watch my back.

1049
01:35:39,948 --> 01:35:41,658
You have two choices.

1050
01:35:41,742 --> 01:35:44,453
I know you hate your father as much as I do.

1051
01:35:44,536 --> 01:35:47,289
So you and I,

1052
01:35:48,165 --> 01:35:51,668
and young Dmitri, will work together.

1053
01:35:51,752 --> 01:35:53,378
You can be my partners.

1054
01:35:53,462 --> 01:35:55,506
Or I'll kill you and...

1055
01:36:01,011 --> 01:36:02,429
Whatever you like.

1056
01:36:02,971 --> 01:36:05,432
Let's hunt the Hunter.

1057
01:36:22,157 --> 01:36:23,575
Split up.

1058
01:36:24,743 --> 01:36:26,412
Bring me his body.

1059
01:36:27,496 --> 01:36:29,164
Or don't come back.

1060
01:36:49,059 --> 01:36:50,102
Raja.

1061
01:36:55,065 --> 01:36:56,191
Where is he?

1062
01:36:57,568 --> 01:36:58,819
He's here.

1063
01:37:00,696 --> 01:37:02,573
Hey! Watch out!

1064
01:38:08,931 --> 01:38:11,975
Amateurs. They make us look bad.

1065
01:38:13,393 --> 01:38:14,228
Do it.

1066
01:38:16,897 --> 01:38:17,898
Fly over them.

1067
01:38:28,450 --> 01:38:30,077
Fire at will.

1068
01:38:30,869 --> 01:38:32,371
No, it isn't real.

1069
01:39:19,543 --> 01:39:21,462
The spiders!

1070
01:39:37,478 --> 01:39:40,105
The hallucinations are only the beginning.

1071
01:39:41,774 --> 01:39:44,234
Can you see your worst nightmare?

1072
01:39:46,612 --> 01:39:47,613
One.

1073
01:39:49,406 --> 01:39:50,407
Two.

1074
01:39:52,743 --> 01:39:53,577
Three.

1075
01:39:59,458 --> 01:40:02,711
As the poison moves toward your spinal cord,

1076
01:40:02,795 --> 01:40:05,798
you'll begin to lose motor function.

1077
01:40:05,881 --> 01:40:07,424
And then, asphyxiation.

1078
01:40:08,050 --> 01:40:09,593
You're the legend?

1079
01:40:11,470 --> 01:40:12,763
The myth?

1080
01:40:15,808 --> 01:40:17,226
But look at you now.

1081
01:40:17,309 --> 01:40:18,644
You're just a man.

1082
01:40:55,097 --> 01:40:56,932
Tear him apart, Kraven.

1083
01:41:12,531 --> 01:41:14,575
I swear, I thought this would be harder.

1084
01:41:18,495 --> 01:41:19,872
It's done.

1085
01:41:19,955 --> 01:41:21,832
But the brother's still out there.

1086
01:41:21,915 --> 01:41:23,417
Find him.

1087
01:41:23,500 --> 01:41:24,501
Let's go.

1088
01:41:27,254 --> 01:41:28,255
One.

1089
01:41:29,548 --> 01:41:30,549
Two.

1090
01:41:33,677 --> 01:41:35,262
Three, motherfucker.

1091
01:41:35,345 --> 01:41:37,598
Goodbye, Kraven the Hunter.

1092
01:41:42,519 --> 01:41:43,896
Sergei!

1093
01:41:48,442 --> 01:41:50,360
Nothing ever goes your way, does it?

1094
01:42:15,219 --> 01:42:17,721
Legends never die.

1095
01:42:17,805 --> 01:42:19,973
Come on, get up, Kraven.

1096
01:42:36,532 --> 01:42:38,409
I knew you had more of that.

1097
01:42:38,492 --> 01:42:41,829
Well, forgive me for not trusting a lunatic

1098
01:42:41,912 --> 01:42:43,997
with my family's greatest legacy.

1099
01:42:45,374 --> 01:42:46,375
Get up.

1100
01:42:47,418 --> 01:42:48,293
Okay.

1101
01:42:52,172 --> 01:42:54,216
Those were some good summer classes.

1102
01:42:54,800 --> 01:42:56,927
You're not the only one with secrets.

1103
01:42:57,719 --> 01:42:59,596
Don't make me regret this.

1104
01:43:09,815 --> 01:43:11,275
It's over.

1105
01:43:12,192 --> 01:43:13,318
Kraven is dead.

1106
01:43:19,825 --> 01:43:21,243
What a day.

1107
01:43:28,000 --> 01:43:29,501
Put him in the car.

1108
01:43:30,836 --> 01:43:34,923
I don't know, maybe Nikolai will pay now that
he only has one son left.

1109
01:43:53,984 --> 01:43:56,528
Does anyone else see

1110
01:43:56,612 --> 01:43:58,739
what I'm seeing?

1111
01:44:59,091 --> 01:45:01,218
Kraven!

1112
01:45:12,438 --> 01:45:13,689
You're so heavy.

1113
01:45:57,107 --> 01:45:58,400
Sergei.

1114
01:47:01,338 --> 01:47:03,715
My father was right about one thing.

1115
01:47:04,883 --> 01:47:06,385
You're nothing.

1116
01:48:10,365 --> 01:48:12,493
That video of me, who gave it to you?

1117
01:48:15,496 --> 01:48:16,622
Who sent it?

1118
01:48:18,415 --> 01:48:22,169
Who would've thought even the great Hunter

1119
01:48:22,252 --> 01:48:27,508
couldn't see what was right in front of him
all along?

1120
01:48:39,436 --> 01:48:40,521
No.

1121
01:48:42,272 --> 01:48:44,400
He deserves to die.

1122
01:48:44,483 --> 01:48:45,484
And he will.

1123
01:48:46,610 --> 01:48:48,445
But Dmitri, that's not who you are.

1124
01:49:02,584 --> 01:49:03,669
I wish...

1125
01:49:05,754 --> 01:49:07,714
I wish I'd never met...

1126
01:49:08,882 --> 01:49:11,093
the Kravinoffs.

1127
01:49:23,439 --> 01:49:28,277
NORTHERN RUSSIA

1128
01:49:51,133 --> 01:49:52,176
Sergei.

1129
01:49:53,051 --> 01:49:54,052
How did you find me?

1130
01:49:55,387 --> 01:49:56,722
I'm a hunter.

1131
01:49:58,223 --> 01:50:01,143
It's what we do.

1132
01:50:04,521 --> 01:50:06,231
You gave him the video

1133
01:50:06,982 --> 01:50:09,860
and told Rhino who I was.

1134
01:50:11,820 --> 01:50:13,822
Did you really think

1135
01:50:13,906 --> 01:50:17,201
a father wouldn't recognize his own son's
handiwork?

1136
01:50:17,910 --> 01:50:22,998
A killer who uses every method of the animals
in the jungle.

1137
01:50:25,167 --> 01:50:29,004
You, of all people, should recognize and
appreciate

1138
01:50:29,088 --> 01:50:30,964
the beauty of the trap I set.

1139
01:50:35,177 --> 01:50:37,513
Rhino was coming for you.

1140
01:50:38,597 --> 01:50:41,558
And you don't have the strength to fight him
alone, do you?

1141
01:50:41,642 --> 01:50:43,102
Exactly.

1142
01:50:43,769 --> 01:50:45,229
But my son,

1143
01:50:45,813 --> 01:50:47,564
my true son,

1144
01:50:47,648 --> 01:50:48,732
Kraven...

1145
01:50:50,359 --> 01:50:52,111
No one is stronger.

1146
01:50:53,445 --> 01:50:55,072
And I knew

1147
01:50:56,115 --> 01:50:58,617
you wouldn't go after him for me.

1148
01:51:00,661 --> 01:51:02,538
So I sent him after you.

1149
01:51:04,123 --> 01:51:05,749
Quite a trap.

1150
01:51:08,669 --> 01:51:11,797
Dmitri could have died, but that's the price
of your business.

1151
01:51:11,880 --> 01:51:13,465
No, no, no.

1152
01:51:13,549 --> 01:51:15,092
Because I know

1153
01:51:15,843 --> 01:51:19,721
you'd never let anything happen to our
precious Dmitri.

1154
01:51:21,390 --> 01:51:23,684
Our empire is safe.

1155
01:51:23,767 --> 01:51:25,394
So what now?

1156
01:51:25,477 --> 01:51:27,062
Dad, do we forget...

1157
01:51:28,939 --> 01:51:30,691
the past?

1158
01:51:31,275 --> 01:51:33,902
Imagine a future together?

1159
01:51:35,487 --> 01:51:36,864
As a family.

1160
01:51:51,712 --> 01:51:52,546
Sergei!

1161
01:51:53,297 --> 01:51:54,548
Where are you going?

1162
01:52:00,429 --> 01:52:02,139
I could've come for you...

1163
01:52:03,807 --> 01:52:05,100
years ago.

1164
01:52:06,477 --> 01:52:07,770
But I didn't.

1165
01:52:09,396 --> 01:52:10,939
Despite what you've done...

1166
01:52:11,940 --> 01:52:14,359
all the suffering you bring into the world,

1167
01:52:16,945 --> 01:52:18,739
you were my father.

1168
01:52:20,324 --> 01:52:21,617
I still am.

1169
01:52:23,368 --> 01:52:24,536
Sit down.

1170
01:52:38,092 --> 01:52:39,760
"Don't fear death."

1171
01:52:41,553 --> 01:52:43,514
Isn't that what you taught me?

1172
01:53:22,886 --> 01:53:26,640
ONE YEAR LATER

1173
01:54:00,382 --> 01:54:01,592
Happy birthday, Dima.

1174
01:54:02,551 --> 01:54:03,927
It is a happy birthday.

1175
01:54:05,763 --> 01:54:06,930
The first in a long time.

1176
01:54:08,307 --> 01:54:09,767
Thanks to you, Sergei.

1177
01:54:10,392 --> 01:54:11,351
Oh, please.

1178
01:54:11,435 --> 01:54:13,228
- Or Kraven, I should say.
- No.

1179
01:54:13,312 --> 01:54:15,439
What should I call you now? Mr. Kraven?

1180
01:54:15,522 --> 01:54:16,815
You know who I am.

1181
01:54:16,899 --> 01:54:18,150
I know you.

1182
01:54:21,236 --> 01:54:22,613
What I went through was...

1183
01:54:23,155 --> 01:54:24,406
hell.

1184
01:54:24,490 --> 01:54:26,033
What I suffered.

1185
01:54:26,116 --> 01:54:28,827
But it also... set me free.

1186
01:54:30,162 --> 01:54:33,707
I feel reborn.

1187
01:54:35,459 --> 01:54:38,295
I found a doctor in New York.

1188
01:54:38,378 --> 01:54:41,131
Not exactly conventional, to be honest.

1189
01:54:43,133 --> 01:54:46,303
But he really helped me. I mean...

1190
01:54:47,846 --> 01:54:49,264
he changed me.

1191
01:54:50,474 --> 01:54:52,643
- How?
- One second.

1192
01:55:01,693 --> 01:55:03,862
Since when do you have friends in the bratva?

1193
01:55:03,946 --> 01:55:06,782
- I do business with a lot of people.
- Business?

1194
01:55:06,865 --> 01:55:09,785
Didn't you want to sell all of Dad's assets
and leave the business?

1195
01:55:09,868 --> 01:55:11,286
I changed my mind.

1196
01:55:11,370 --> 01:55:14,581
I didn't save you from hell so you could
become like Dad.

1197
01:55:14,665 --> 01:55:16,041
Are you serious?

1198
01:55:16,125 --> 01:55:18,544
You're the one who put me through that hell.

1199
01:55:18,627 --> 01:55:20,129
You're just like Dad.

1200
01:55:20,212 --> 01:55:22,923
I'm nothing like him. I have a code.

1201
01:55:23,006 --> 01:55:24,091
And you're different?

1202
01:55:24,174 --> 01:55:25,717
- I'm better than him.
- You're...

1203
01:55:25,801 --> 01:55:27,553
You're not better than him.

1204
01:55:27,636 --> 01:55:29,096
You're worse.

1205
01:55:30,055 --> 01:55:31,974
How did you say Dad died?

1206
01:55:33,934 --> 01:55:36,228
A hunting accident.

1207
01:55:36,311 --> 01:55:37,146
Right?

1208
01:55:37,771 --> 01:55:39,148
Don't lie to me.

1209
01:55:40,357 --> 01:55:42,818
You think you have honor, huh?

1210
01:55:43,402 --> 01:55:44,570
A code?

1211
01:55:45,487 --> 01:55:46,572
Give me a break.

1212
01:55:47,698 --> 01:55:53,579
You're just another man who hunts for trophies.

1213
01:56:02,713 --> 01:56:03,797
Hey!

1214
01:56:06,842 --> 01:56:08,093
Dmitri...

1215
01:56:16,059 --> 01:56:18,604
You should've seen the look on your face.

1216
01:56:27,780 --> 01:56:28,781
Hey!

1217
01:56:32,618 --> 01:56:33,660
Dmitri.

1218
01:56:34,620 --> 01:56:35,954
You know me.

1219
01:56:36,663 --> 01:56:38,207
I've always been a chameleon.

1220
01:56:40,042 --> 01:56:42,878
It's the one thing I've always been good at.

1221
01:56:42,961 --> 01:56:46,006
Who is that doctor? What did he do to you?

1222
01:56:46,090 --> 01:56:47,966
You want me to be weak

1223
01:56:48,050 --> 01:56:50,719
so you can always be stronger. But I'm strong now.

1224
01:56:52,304 --> 01:56:54,056
I can be whoever I want.

1225
01:56:54,139 --> 01:56:56,850
Rhino is dead. Dad is dead.

1226
01:56:56,934 --> 01:56:58,477
It's all there

1227
01:56:59,269 --> 01:57:00,896
for the taking.

1228
01:57:02,314 --> 01:57:03,899
And I'm going to take it.

1229
01:57:08,570 --> 01:57:10,531
I can't let you do that.

1230
01:57:14,993 --> 01:57:16,703
Go home, Kraven.

1231
01:57:21,708 --> 01:57:23,293
Dad left you something.

1232
01:57:57,494 --> 01:57:59,121
Sergei...

1233
01:57:59,204 --> 01:58:01,540
everyone has a path to walk.

1234
01:58:03,000 --> 01:58:05,502
Accept who you truly are,

1235
01:58:05,586 --> 01:58:07,671
and you'll have the strength to walk it.

1236
01:58:09,214 --> 01:58:11,425
You're more than my son.

1237
01:58:13,135 --> 01:58:13,969
You are me...

1238
01:58:16,346 --> 01:58:18,140
and I am you.

1239
01:58:23,771 --> 01:58:25,481
We are hunters...

1240
01:58:27,649 --> 01:58:30,652
the best the world has ever seen.

1241
02:06:30,883 --> 02:06:32,885
TRANSLATION: MIGUEL EDUARDO REYES ALDASORO
